// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - TheFamily_Portal_Brawl_Thug 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1236391004" "Organized crime has always had plenty of competition in Paragon City, but that doesn't stop young street toughs from wanting to swear allegiance to their Don and live like a wiseguy. The Button Man Brawlers are amongst the toughest of the lower ranking Family thugs. They use stolen technology to make each of their punches hit like a ton of bricks. Their brass knuckles are also poisoned with a rare toxin. The Family only calls on these thugs when it's necessary, as they are normally away on important business."
// DisplayNames :
"P2548314363" "Button Man Brawler"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - TheFamily_Portal_Shotgun_Thug 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P4047233446" "Organized crime has always had plenty of competition in Paragon City, but that doesn't stop young street toughs from wanting to swear allegiance to their Don and live like a wiseguy. The Button Man 'Beamers' carry around stolen beam rifle technology, most likely from Crey, or even Malta. The Family is willing to go to great lengths to ensure their empire is kept safe."
// DisplayNames :
"P2833469669" "Button Man Beamer"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - TheFamily_Portal_SubmachineGun_Thug 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3269007745" "Organized crime has always had plenty of competition in Paragon City, but that doesn't stop young street toughs from wanting to swear allegiance to their Don and live like a wiseguy. The Button Man Hitters are pinpoint shots with their heavily modified guns."
// DisplayNames :
"P3099107792" "Button Man Hitter"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - TheFamily_Portal_Muscle_Lieutenant 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2950374979" "Each Capo controls his own crew of Button Men. It's a kind of authority you don't earn unless you've proven yourself both ruthless and lucky. Capos save the best weapons and women for themselves and are inevitably smart, tough fighters. The Capo Strongarm is among the strongest of the Capos. They've been seen throwing rival mafia's cars to deal with 'problems' that arise. One thing is clear: you don't mess with a Capo Strongarm."
// DisplayNames :
"P2436986792" "Capo Strongarm"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - TheFamily_Portal_AssaultRifle_Lieutenant 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P21149744" "Each Capo controls his own crew of Button Men. It's a kind of authority you don't earn unless you've proven yourself both ruthless and lucky. Capos save the best weapons and women for themselves and are inevitably smart, tough fighters. These Capos have been given the honor of using stolen Praetorian technology, specifically the Resistance Heavy Barrels. The Family had a choice in the matter; they could take the Resistance rifles, or the Resistance Heavy Barrels. Once the capos saw the Heavy Barrel in action, their decision was a no brainer."
// DisplayNames :
"P1993296862" "Capo Heavy"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - TheFamily_Portal_Underboss_Boss 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3320925786" "The Prima Capo is the 'Head Capo' and reports directly to the Don. In Paragon City, you don't rise to the top without a little super-powered help, and many Underbosses have heightened abilities or access to specialized gear that helps them stay on top in their cutthroat business. Some Prima Capos have become so strong that they carry around a huge chunk of concrete to show their opponents 'who is the real boss around here'. They're able to swing these huge weapons with ease and use them for intimidation, though usually it's used to bash in someone's head."
// DisplayNames :
"P2447455192" "Prima Capo"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - TheFamily_Portal_Consigliere_Boss 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P956112266" "In Paragon City, you don't become one of the Don's trusted advisors without a little super-powered expertise. Consiglieres have far more subtle powers than their Underboss counterparts, which match their more subtle responsibilities within the Family. The highest of the Consiglieres have modified their abilities to also heal their fellow mafioso around them. The Consiglieres are dangerous on their own, but they're even more powerful when they're around their goons."
// DisplayNames :
"P3116863932" "Prima Consigliere"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - TheFamily_Underboss_Span_NoAuto 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2907569319" "The Prima Capo is the 'Head Capo' and report directly to the Don. In Paragon City, you don't rise to the top without a little super-powered help, and many Underbosses have heightened abilities or access to specialized gear that helps them stay on top in their cutthroat business. Some Prima Capos have become so strong that they carry around a huge chunk of concrete to show their opponents 'who is the real boss around here'. They're able to swing these huge weapons with ease and use them for intimidation, though usually it's used to bash in someone's head."

